    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d51-a7">

                <pb facs="0162" n="58" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg58"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No. 143.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Houston to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pacific Mail Steamship Company</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-01"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 1, 1890</date>.
                        (Received August 2.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Inclosed please find copy of a letter
                    dated 31st ultimo received by this company to-day from the consul-general of
                    Guatemala in New York, Mr. Jacob Baiz.</p>
                <p>Also copy of our reply to the same of even date. We forward this correspondence
                    in compliance with the request of the Honorable Mr. Adee, that the Department of
                    State should be furnished with all information bearing on this case.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Houston</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">President</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
